# Repository Workflow Rules

## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Two Separate Repositories - ALWAYS VERIFY BEFORE PUSHING

This project uses TWO separate GitHub repositories. **MISTAKES HERE BREAK THE DEPLOYMENT.**

1. **divine-link** (`https://github.com/ayoola66/divine-link.git`)
   - Contains: App source code (Swift files, Xcode project)
   - Location: Root workspace directory
   - Remote: `origin`

2. **divine-link-site** (`https://github.com/ayoola66/divine-link-site.git`)
   - Contains: Netlify website files (admin.html, landing pages)
   - Location: `Distribution/netlify-site/` directory
   - Deploys to: https://divinelink.netlify.app
   - Remote: `netlify-site` (if configured) OR clone separately

## MANDATORY VERIFICATION CHECKLIST

**BEFORE EVERY PUSH, YOU MUST:**

1. ✅ **Identify which files changed:**
   ```bash
   git status --short
   ```

2. ✅ **Check file locations:**
   - Files in `Distribution/netlify-site/` → `divine-link-site` repo
   - All other files → `divine-link` repo

3. ✅ **Verify target repository:**
   ```bash
   # For divine-link-site files:
   git remote -v | grep "divine-link-site"
   
   # For divine-link files:
   git remote -v | grep "divine-link.git"
   ```

4. ✅ **Confirm before pushing:**
   - Show user: "Pushing [file list] to [repository name]"
   - Wait for confirmation if uncertain

## Rules for Pushing Changes

### ALWAYS Check File Location First

**Before pushing ANY changes:**

1. **Check if file is in `Distribution/netlify-site/`:**
   - ✅ YES → **MUST** push to `divine-link-site` repository
   - ❌ NO → Push to `divine-link` repository

### Files That Go to `divine-link-site`:

- `Distribution/netlify-site/admin.html` ⚠️ **CRITICAL**
- `Distribution/netlify-site/index.html`
- `Distribution/netlify-site/appcast.xml`
- `Distribution/netlify-site/*.html` (all HTML files)
- `Distribution/netlify-site/netlify.toml`
- `Distribution/netlify-site/releases/*` (app ZIP files)

### Files That Go to `divine-link`:

- All Swift files (`DivineLink/**/*.swift`)
- Xcode project files
- Documentation (`docs/`, `README.md`)
- Database schemas (`Distribution/supabase-*.sql`)
- All other files NOT in `Distribution/netlify-site/`

## SAFE Workflow for Admin/Website Changes

**When modifying files in `Distribution/netlify-site/`:**

### Option 1: Use the Sync Script (RECOMMENDED)

```bash
# Run the sync script with a commit message
"/Users/ayoogunrekun/Projects/Divine Link/scripts/sync-netlify-site.sh" "Your commit message"
```

### Option 2: Manual Sync

```bash
# STEP 1: Copy file(s) to the local divine-link-site repo
cp "/Users/ayoogunrekun/Projects/Divine Link/Distribution/netlify-site/admin.html" \
   /Users/ayoogunrekun/Projects/divine-link-site/

# STEP 2: Commit and push from divine-link-site
cd /Users/ayoogunrekun/Projects/divine-link-site
git add -A
git commit -m "Description"
git push origin main
```

### ⚠️ NEVER use /tmp clones - they don't have your Git credentials!

## Verification Before Pushing

**ALWAYS verify:**
- [ ] File location checked (`Distribution/netlify-site/`?)
- [ ] Correct repository identified (show remote URL)
- [ ] Changes committed
- [ ] Pushing to correct remote (verify URL)
- [ ] User notified of which repo is being pushed to

## Error Prevention

**NEVER:**
- ❌ Push `Distribution/netlify-site/*` files to `divine-link` repo
- ❌ Assume - always verify remote URL
- ❌ Skip verification steps

**ALWAYS:**
- ✅ Check file location first
- ✅ Verify remote URL before pushing
- ✅ Use the sync script or local divine-link-site repo
- ✅ Show user which repo you're pushing to

